      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "If this was a thing it should be toggleable, because as soon as you got a lag spike (very common in VRC) you would be kicked from the world",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-07-26T09:00:09.404Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The idea is simple: If the frame rate becomes too low for any reason, VRChat should send you to a safe space where avatar and world processing is suspended. This safe space should offer the option to head to your home world if desired. It should also offer the option to return back to the world from the safe space (potentially disabling further \"low framerate\" notifications until the user switches worlds), just in case the low framerate is tolerable or the \"low framerate detection\" was tripped via a false positive.\n\nThe intention behind this suggestion is to combat worlds that are unoptimized or laggy (deliberately or not). It's especially meant to allow VR users to escape low framerate situations that may otherwise require force-quitting the game (such as on Quest where extremely low framerates can actually prevent the rest of the system from responding).",
